ba6e7bdd7d63787567bf4094410121d"},"seconds":47.2988440990448,"seed":167653886412556167,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the seventh term of the geometric sequence, we start by recalling the general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of a geometric sequence, which is given by:\n\n\\[a_n = a_1 \\cdot r^{n-1}\\]\n\nwhere \\(a_1\\) is the first term, \\(r\\) is the common ratio, and \\(n\\) is the term number.\n\nGiven:\n- The third term \\(a_3 = 1053\\)\n- The ninth term \\(a_9 = \\frac{13}{9}\\)\n\nUsing the general formula, we can express these terms as follows:\n\\[a_3 = a_1 \\cdot r^2 = 1053\\]\n\\[a_9 = a_1 \\cdot r^8 = \\frac{13}{9}\\]\n\nWe can solve for \\(a_1\\) in terms of \\(r\\) from the equation for \\(a_3\\):\n\\[a_1 = \\frac{1053}{r^2}\\]\n\nNow substitute this expression for \\(a_1\\) into the equation for \\(a_9\\):\n\\[\\frac{1053}{r^2} \\cdot r^8 = \\frac{13}{9}\\]\n\\[1053 \\cdot r^6 = \\frac{13}{9}\\]\n\\[r^6 = \\frac{13}{9 \\cdot 1053}\\]\n\\[r^6 = \\frac{13}{9477}\\]\n\\[r^6 = \\frac{1}{729}\\]\n\\[r^6 = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^6\\]\n\\[r = \\frac{1}{3} \\text{ or } r = -\\frac{1}{3}\\]\n\nWe will consider both cases.\n\n**Case 1: \\(r = \\frac{1}{3}\\)**\n\nSubstitute \\(r = \\frac{1}{3}\\) back into the expression for \\(a_1\\):\n\\[a_1 = \\frac{1053}{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2} = \\frac{1053}{\\frac{1}{9}} = 1053 \\cdot 9 = 9477\\]\n\nNow, we can find the seventh term \\(a_7\\):\n\\[a_7 = a_1 \\cdot r^6 = 9477 \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^6 = 9477 \\cdot \\frac{1}{729} = 13\\]\n\n**Case 2: \\(r = -\\frac{1}{3}\\)**\n\nSubstitute \\(r = -\\frac{1}{3}\\) back into the expression for \\(a_1\\):\n\\[a_1 = \\frac{1053}{\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^2} = \\frac{1053}{\\frac{1}{9}} = 1053 \\cdot 9 = 9477\\]\n\nNow, we can find the seventh term \\(a_7\\):\n\\[a_7 = a_1 \\cdot r^6 = 9477 \\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^6 = 9477 \\cdot \\frac{1}{729} = 13\\]\n\nIn both cases, the seventh term is the same. Therefore, the value of the seventh term is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{13}\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{13}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
